I stumbled accross this issue when looking for a way to get the information from the package.json file to create the base command setup. Using the `findPackageJSON` seems to work nicely.

I did the following to test whether it works, and this gives the desired result for me:

```typescript
import { findPackageJSON } from 'node:module';
import { readFileSync } from 'fs';

// Find the package.json path and fetch the needed properties.
const packageJsonPath = findPackageJSON('..', import.meta.url);
const { name, version, description } = JSON.parse(readFileSync(packageJsonPath!, 'utf-8'));

// Create the program with information from the package.json file.
const program = new Command();
program
   .name(name)
   .description(description)
   .version(version);
```

In my case I am sure all properties are there, but in a generic implementation some more exception handling is needed.

I am wondering whether this is the right approach, any thoughts?
